{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_41_790233410#6_1705832934","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage is about war-related inflation and specifically notes that Vietnam War inflation was not followed by a decline in prices, but it is a broad investment/inflation discussion rather than dedicated to the Vietnam War economy in 1968 or its severity.","learned":"Vietnam was among wars where wartime inflation did not reverse; prices continued climbing after the war-inflation period."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"guns and butter\" \"vietnam war\" (+ inflation deficit 1968 economy))","reason":"The phrase 'guns and butter' is a common label for Johnson-era Vietnam plus Great Society fiscal pressure and should retrieve focused economic-history evidence."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"guns and butter\" \"vietnam war\" (+ inflation deficit 1968 economy))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_30_346287628#0_805117561","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1202","rank":1,"snippet":"damaged the U.S. economy severely. The U.S. had poured some $168 billion into the war, but the real cost of the conflict was its impact on the economy. After a few truly good years during 1962 – 1965 when there was low inflation, almost full employment and a favorable balance of trade, President Lyndon B. Johnson, who succeeded President Kennedy after his assassination in 1963, declared a “War on Poverty” through his “Great Society” programs while escalating the war in Vietnam at the same time. However, his decision to finance both “<cover>guns and butter” – a major war and the Great Society simultaneously, without a significant increase in taxes unleashed an acceleration of inflation peaking at a runaway double-digit in mid 1970s. Not until 1969 did President Johnson decided to introduce a 10% income tax surcharge, which is considered by many economists “too little and too late” and in turn also slowed down the economy.\" , \"start_char\": 0.000000 , \"title\": \"How did the Vietnam War </cover>affect America? - The Vietnam War\" , \"url\": \"https://thevietnamwar.info/how-vietnam-war-affect-america/\" }"}}
