{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_590172108#3_1022720351","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage gives precise 1968 economic evidence tied to Johnson's Vietnam War and Great Society spending: growth of 4.9%, inflation of 4.7%, a huge balance-of-payments deficit, and pressure on the gold standard. However, the document is mainly about Nixon's economic policies and the dollar, not dedicated to the Vietnam War's economic devastation in 1968.","learned":"In 1968, Vietnam War and Great Society spending boosted growth to 4.9% but pushed inflation to 4.7%, worsened the balance-of-payments deficit, and threatened the gold standard."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1205","reason":"This query is producing 1968-specific quantitative economic evidence; continue to find more direct sources connecting Vietnam War spending with inflation, deficits, and economic stress."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1205"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_03_590172108#2_1022718879","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1205","rank":2,"snippet":"Created the 1973-1975 Recession Nixon's Other Economic Impacts Nixon Doctrine Watergate Nixon's Early Years Nixon Presidency by Year Other Presidents' Economic Policies Article Sources \" , \"segment\": \"That move bypassed America's free-market economy. Even worse, Nixon ended the gold standard that tied the dollar's value to gold. This move created a decade of stagflation. It was only cured by double-digit interest rates, causing the devastating 1981 recession. Ending the gold standard permitted the U.S. government to print dollars to solve every economic woe. That ensured the dollar's value would fall indefinitely. How did that happen? Balance of Payments <cover>Deficit In 1968, President Johnson's spending on the Vietnam War and the Great Society boosted economic growth to 4.9%. 3 ﻿ But it sent inflation </cover>to a disturbing 4.7%. 4 ﻿ As Americans prospered, they imported more goods, paying in dollars.\" , \"start_char\": 1369.000000 , \"title\": \"President Richard M. Nixon's Economic Policies\" , \"url\": \"http://useconomy.about.com/od/Politics/fl/President-Richard-M-Nixons-Economic-Policies.htm\" }"}}
