{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_317254117#27_726862189","relevance":3,"reason":"This segment is from a dedicated Vietnam War facts/costs/effects article and directly supports the information need: it says Vietnam War spending helped boost the economy but also played a role in causing the Great Inflation beginning in 1965, alongside LBJ's War on Poverty and other social programs.","learned":"Vietnam War spending was a contributor to the Great Inflation beginning in 1965, though the source says it was only a small part compared with other LBJ spending too."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1229","reason":"This query produced a dedicated grade-3 economic-effects segment; continue for additional segments or unique sources linking Vietnam War spending, Great Inflation, Johnson, taxes, and the economy."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1229"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_27_550642880#3_1118169262","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1229","rank":3,"snippet":"the Korean War. The most recent spike in inflation occurred during the Great Inflation. The Great Inflation, which started in the mid-1960s, lasted for almost two decades and only began to dissipate in the early 1980s. During that time, the inflation rate soared from a mere 1.6 percent in 1965 to 13.5 percent in 1980 (see top chart). Inflation has been relatively tame since its rapid decline in the early 1980s; the highest rate observed was only 5.5 percent during the commodity price boom in July 2008. Certain economists attribute the <cover>Great Inflation primarily to monetary policy mistakes rather than other purported causes, such as high oil prices and defense spending during the Vietnam War. </cover>In the 1960s, Fed officials—and prominent economists—generally believed expansionary monetary policy could propel the economy toward full employment.\" , \"start_char\": 2432.000000 , \"title\": \"The Great Inflation: A Historical Overview and Lessons Learned - Page One Economics® - St. Louis Fed\" , \"url\": \"https://research.stlouisfed.org/publications/page1-econ/2012/10/01/the-great-inflation-a-historical-overview-and-lessons-learned/\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_317254117#28_726863651","rank":2,"relevance":3}]}}
